.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt SC101IOTS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sc101iots
.Nd SC101IOT sensor identification
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "sc101iots* at iic? addr 0x68"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver identifies a SmartSens SC101IOT image sensor over SCCB/I2C.
It asserts reset and power-down while acquiring the controls, enables the
referenced shared supply, waits for the module-provided external oscillator,
then releases power-down and reset before reading the sensor ID.
The driver leaves the sensor in reset and power-down after probing.
It never disables the shared supply.
.Pp
The device-tree node uses compatible string
.Dq smartsens,sc101iot
and supplies
.Va reg , reset-gpios , powerdown-gpios , power-supply
properties.
Its 7-bit I2C address is 0x68.
The sensor uses paged 8-bit register access: the driver writes the page
number to register 0xf0, then reads the low register byte.
It reads registers 0x31f7 and 0x31f8 and expects ID 0xda4a.
.Pp
The module provides its own XCLK.
The operating system does not control or declare a fixed frequency for that
oscillator.
It waits 20 ms before SCCB access; this delay does not assert a measured
frequency.
The optional module node is enabled by the
.Pa ESP_MOSAICO_SC101IOT
configuration.
The base
.Pa ESP_MOSAICO
tree leaves it disabled.
The OV3640 camera variant remains separate.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
This driver only identifies the SC101IOT sensor.
It does not configure image formats, attach a video device, or capture
frames.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iic 4 ,
.Xr ov3640s 4
